 Oh [Music]  beautiful day bit somber yeah  so quick video what's this this is a  journal or gratitude journal what  everyone will call it and I wanted to  make a video because this is the third  year now that I've kept a journal and I  think that it can benefit loads of  people if you don't have one so two main  reasons why or the benefits i've seen  from keeping a journal so firstly we're  all guilty of this and that's sort of  just holding on to how you're feeling  about something if you're angry it's  something or you're upset you're sad or  whatever it is you're holding on to it  and sometimes you feel like there's no  outlet besides maybe getting emotional  or having an argument with someone or  whatever and what this has really helped  me with is BL but there's something  about writing it down that is really  really powerful so when I felt maybe  some of those emotions and I felt sad  about certain things or upset or  whatever writing it down in this journal  really feels like you've got it off your  chest  and that helps a lot so that's the first  thing  secondly it's so easy to if you were to  say to me hisham what happened sort of  last year or what sort of how did last  year go I find that really hard it all  sort of just merges into one and what  this journal allows you to do is what  I've done for the last two years now is  as it is going on if you really wanted  to you could sort of take the time one  day a month to sort of just look through  your mum see how it's going for you see  where you can make improvements or what  you'll please we have all those sorts of  things but what's been really really  powerful is being able to look at my  whole year through sort of my entries  into my journal and you can get some  really really cool insights when you  have access to that  so with that as well it's so easy just  to forget sort of how far you've come  sometimes because you're you're thinking  about where you are now you didn't you  sometimes hard to really live or think  about where you was 12 months ago and  when you read passages from 12 months  ago you can sort of get into that  mindset of what you was that time or  what you as feeling and one I think  that's a great thing to be able to do to  go to make sure that you're sort of  taking the right steps and also as I  said some really really cool insights  you can get from reading your journal so  if you haven't got a journal I'd really  really recommend it there's no secret to  sort of what you have to write or  whatever just write how you feel right  how that day's gone maybe what you're  grateful for on that day and honestly  it's great it's a great great simple  tool to have and honestly I feel like a  lot of people could benefit from it  [Music]


